# 069 · Copy a campaign

**Status:** `VERIFIED` · **Version:** [v0.1.0](../../roadmap.md#v010) · **Part:** Running campaigns

## What

A copy of a campaign: a new campaign with another name, the same contract and the same kit as the source's newest saved version or, for a campaign control knows only by an assignment, as that assignment.

- **Its name.** The contract names the copy, so the copy's contract hash is its own.
- **Its folder.** It has its own folder in Thermite's knowledge base, which starts empty. It reads no other folder, and no folder is granted to it.
- **No runs.** It starts with Start a run, as any campaign does: REST `POST /v1/campaigns/<name>/runs`, MCP `start_run`, `thermite run start` or the campaign's page.
- **Its history.** Control records who copied it and from which campaign (and which version) in its audit log, and the copy's page shows it.
- **Where.** **Copy** on the campaign's page, REST `POST /v1/campaigns/<name>/copy`, MCP `copy_campaign` and `thermite campaign copy <from> <new-name>`.

## Why

The owner wants to compare two models on the same research campaign, both from zero. Two runs of one campaign share its folder in the knowledge base: each starts with what earlier runs recorded, and each reads the other's records every few minutes. Thermite had no way to make a second campaign with the same settings and an empty folder, except to type the whole New campaign form again.

## Done when

- [x] REST `POST /v1/campaigns/<name>/copy`, MCP `copy_campaign` and `thermite campaign copy` copy a campaign, and refuse in words: no saved version and no assignment, a name that is taken or not valid, a rig check's campaign.
- [x] The copy's contract names the copy and has its own hash; its folder is empty, with no grants; it has no runs, and Start a run starts it. Its run reads only the copy's folder.
- [x] Who copied it, from which campaign and version, is in the audit log and on the copy's page.
- [x] Only the owner's token (REST, the command line, MCP) and the operator's (MCP) may copy. A reader's or an agent's token may not.
- [x] Tests for each surface.
- [x] The REST API, MCP tools and command-line references, the glossary, the knowledge base reference and a how-to section on comparing two models from zero describe it.
- [x] A **Copy** button on the campaign's page, after the owner approves a mockup.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-21, owner: "So you are telling me, we should build a copy function in the future eh?" Then: build it now, over REST, MCP and the command line. The dashboard button comes later, because it needs a mockup.
- 2026-10-21, builder, within the v0.1.0 build brief:
  - **What is copied.** The newest saved version, with its sources (where its runs fetch the project and the kit). For a campaign known only by an assignment: the assignment's contract, and its starting point, imports and MCP servers, kept with the copy so that its runs take them as they are. An assignment's run options (run name, agents, promotion, queue, briefing) are not copied.
  - **The copy's contract.** `campaign` is the new name and `version` is 1; the rest is the source's. Control checks it with the contract check, and saves it as the copy's version 1, approved by whoever copied it.
  - **Taken names.** A name is taken when control knows a campaign by it: a saved version, an assignment, a rig's report, a folder in the knowledge base, or a grant. So the copy's folder is always empty and has no grants. A new name may not start with `rig-check-`, which rig checks use.
  - **Tokens.** As for Start a run: REST and the command line take the owner's token, and MCP takes the owner's and an operator's.
  - **The page.** The copy's page shows one line: `Copied from <campaign> version <n> by <who>, <time> ago. Its folder in the knowledge base started empty.` That is the only screen change in this goal.
- 2026-10-21, owner: approved the mockup of **Copy** on the campaign's page ("Looks good to me"), with its open choices as the mockup showed them:
  - **Copy** is a button beside **Start a run**, not in a menu.
  - The name field starts with a free name: the source's name and `-b`, or the next free letter.
  - After **Copy**, the copy's page opens, with **Start a run** of it.
  - A research copy's MCP servers are listed open in the panel, ticked as the source has them.
  - The copy's line names the owner as "you" (the dashboard is the owner's), and the operator's token as "the operator".

## Open questions

None.

## Progress

- 2026-10-21: Goal written from the owner's decision.
- 2026-10-21: Built over REST, MCP and the command line. `src/control/copy-campaign.ts` copies (through `ControlActions.copyCampaign`, filled in by the dashboard); the store keeps where a copy came from (`campaign_version.copied_from`) and, for a copy of an assignment, that assignment's imports (`sources.assignment`), which Start a run then uses. Tests: `src/control/copy-campaign.test.ts` (a saved campaign and an assignment-only one, the contract's name and hash, the empty folder and no grants, every refusal, the tokens, Start a run on each copy, and the copy's run syncing only its own folder) and `src/cli/campaign.test.ts`. Pages: the REST API, MCP tools, command-line and tokens references, the glossary, the knowledge base reference, and **Compare two models from zero** in Start a campaign from the dashboard. Left: the **Copy** button on the campaign's page, after a mockup.
- 2026-10-21: A research copy may name other MCP servers (owner: relaunch two research campaigns with the agents using a server added in Settings). REST, MCP and `thermite campaign copy --mcp-servers-json FILE` take `mcp_servers` (goal 068's list); the copy's contract names it in place of the source's (`[]`: none), so its hash changes. Checked as on the New campaign page: the server is in Settings and lists each tool named; the kinds of agent are the workers and the advisors (a research run has no planner). A hill-climb or goal campaign is refused in words: its servers are in its kit's kit.json, which a copy does not change. `from.other_mcp_servers`, `campaign_copied`'s `mcp_servers` and a sentence on the copy's page say when the list differs. Tests: `src/control/copy-campaign.test.ts`, `src/cli/campaign.test.ts`. Pages: the MCP tools, REST API and command-line references. Not done: the line on giving copies a server in **Compare two models from zero**, and `--mcp-server NAME` on the command line (only the JSON file).
- 2026-10-21: **Copy** on the campaign's page, as the owner approved its mockup. Beside **Start a run**, it opens a panel (`src/control/ui/copy-campaign.ts`, its script `copy-campaign-client.ts` at `/ui/assets/copy.js`): the copy's name, offered free and checked as you type in control's words, with a fixed name for one that is not valid; for a research campaign, the New campaign page's rows of Settings' MCP servers for the workers and the advisors, ticked as the source has them, with Advanced's tools per kind, a summary, and **Use the servers of … again**; a hill-climb or goal campaign's kit servers, read only; and the same request over REST, MCP and the command line. The form posts without the script (`POST /ui/campaigns/<campaign>/copy`, which sends `mcp_servers` only when they differ from the source's); **Copy** opens the copy's page (`Copied <campaign> version <n> as <copy>.`, then `Copied from … by you, just now.` and **Start a run of** the copy), and a refusal opens the panel again with **Not copied.** and control's words. Every form label has an info icon. Tests: `src/control/copy-ui.test.ts` (the form driven as a browser drives it: a hill-climb copy and its page and run, a research copy with a narrowed and an added server, the source's list kept as it is, refusals for a taken name, a name only a grant has, a name that is not valid, a rig check's name, a server with no agent and a kind with no tool, and no Copy for a rig check) and `src/control/ui/copy-campaign-client.test.ts` (the script's checks against control's own answers). Checked in headless Chrome at desktop and phone widths, light and dark. Pages: **Compare two models from zero** (now from the dashboard, with the research copy's servers and the refusals), the campaign's page in How Thermite fits together, the glossary, the REST API and command-line references, the roadmap and the changelog. Left: `--mcp-server NAME` on the command line (only the JSON file).

